01:15:25.573 --> 01:15:26.406
on the trust system.

01:15:26.406 --> 01:15:28.089
Is this true even for when they, like,

01:15:28.089 --> 01:15:30.859
contact a random Twitter animator

01:15:30.859 --> 01:15:33.392
and ask them to work on a new project?

01:15:33.392 --> 01:15:35.344
It's not under NDA or anything like that?

01:15:35.344 --> 01:15:36.529
- They trust you.

01:15:36.529 --> 01:15:37.362
(Garnt laughs)

01:15:37.362 --> 01:15:39.305
- So, that animator who
could say no and be like,

01:15:39.305 --> 01:15:41.685
"Guys, I know the next
movie that's coming out."

01:15:41.685 --> 01:15:42.518
- Yeah.

01:15:42.518 --> 01:15:43.441
- Oh my God.

01:15:43.441 --> 01:15:46.348
- How has there not been,
like, a leak every week?

01:15:46.348 --> 01:15:50.681
- Because the trust of the
studio and the animators.

01:15:53.461 --> 01:15:57.428
And if you have some leaks,
you can just black list it.

01:15:57.428 --> 01:15:58.503
- Yeah, true, true.

01:15:58.503 --> 01:16:02.154
- And if you get blacklisted
you'd find no more works.

01:16:02.154 --> 01:16:03.112
- Yeah.

01:16:03.112 --> 01:16:04.195
- So, yeah.

01:16:04.195 --> 01:16:05.113
- That's crazy.

01:16:05.113 --> 01:16:06.026
- It's up to you.

01:16:06.026 --> 01:16:07.343
(everyone laughs)

01:16:07.343 --> 01:16:08.242
- Don't fuck it up.

01:16:08.242 --> 01:16:09.700
- Yeah, just don't fuck up.

01:16:09.700 --> 01:16:11.741
- I'm surprised there hasn't
been like just one person,

01:16:11.741 --> 01:16:14.654
one rogue animator hasn't popped up

01:16:14.654 --> 01:16:16.867
in the entire history of anime.

01:16:16.867 --> 01:16:18.776
That's impressive.

01:16:18.776 --> 01:16:23.253
- If you mess up, you're telling
big names what've you done.

01:16:23.253 --> 01:16:25.211
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:16:25.211 --> 01:16:26.419
Jesus.

01:16:26.419 --> 01:16:27.934
- And I guess it would make sense

01:16:27.934 --> 01:16:30.388
'cause a lot of these people
look up to the directors

01:16:30.388 --> 01:16:33.189
and the people in charge, so
I doubt they would try and-

01:16:33.189 --> 01:16:35.025
- I guess it'd be like
backstabbing your idol.

01:16:35.025 --> 01:16:36.708
- Right, the thing that you love.

01:16:36.708 --> 01:16:38.503
So at least that makes sense.

01:16:38.503 --> 01:16:40.628
- I guess, do you want
to talk about the thing

01:16:40.628 --> 01:16:43.431
that all three of us
have been wanting to ask?

01:16:43.431 --> 01:16:46.139
- Yeah, I mean, as an animator on Twitter

01:16:46.139 --> 01:16:47.068
and everything like that.

01:16:47.068 --> 01:16:47.901
- Your opinion matters.

01:16:47.901 --> 01:16:50.495
- Yeah, your opinion matters.

01:16:50.495 --> 01:16:52.171
- Our opinion doesn't mean shit.

01:16:52.171 --> 01:16:55.117
Your opinion on the other
hand, it means a lot.

01:16:55.117 --> 01:16:57.296
- Like, how do you feel about, you know,

01:16:57.296 --> 01:17:00.573
artists and animators getting backlash

01:17:00.573 --> 01:17:02.744
after an episode has aired.

01:17:02.744 --> 01:17:04.328
- [Connor] For example, "Attack on Titan."

01:17:04.328 --> 01:17:05.161
Just say it Garnt.

01:17:05.161 --> 01:17:06.468
(everyone laughs)

01:17:06.468 --> 01:17:07.939
For some reason people
are very, very angry

01:17:07.939 --> 01:17:10.329
and have been sending even,
I think, death threats.

01:17:10.329 --> 01:17:12.904
- Yeah, to directors
and animators on Twitter

01:17:12.904 --> 01:17:13.862
and stuff like that.

01:17:13.862 --> 01:17:15.511
- Does that scare you
or anything like that?

01:17:15.511 --> 01:17:16.506
Working on projects and-

01:17:16.506 --> 01:17:18.660
- Well, if I had those kind of threats,

01:17:18.660 --> 01:17:21.369
I'd be, "Oh, I messed up that."

01:17:21.369 --> 01:17:23.343
(everyone laughs)

01:17:23.343 --> 01:17:24.176
- No, no!

01:17:24.176 --> 01:17:25.969
No, no, you shouldn't feel like that.

01:17:25.969 --> 01:17:29.271
- Actually in my case,
it's just Twitter internet.

01:17:29.271 --> 01:17:31.425
I don't have time to bother about that.

01:17:31.425 --> 01:17:33.036
I have to concentrate on my drawings.

01:17:33.036 --> 01:17:33.990
(everyone laughs)

01:17:33.990 --> 01:17:34.878
- Too busy doing work.

01:17:34.878 --> 01:17:35.711
Yeah, exactly.

01:17:35.711 --> 01:17:38.845
- So, yeah, but for people
who gave up all their guts

01:17:38.845 --> 01:17:43.409
and didn't sleep, managed
to deliver the episode,

01:17:43.409 --> 01:17:46.597
and receive all the threats, it's a bit-

01:17:46.597 --> 01:17:48.145
- I feel like they don't get paid enough

01:17:48.145 --> 01:17:49.455
to deal with threats.

01:17:49.455 --> 01:17:50.649
(everyone laughs)

01:17:50.649 --> 01:17:51.546
You know, hard work.

01:17:51.546 --> 01:17:55.545
- Yeah, and I think most of animators know

01:17:55.545 --> 01:17:57.289
they're working up.

01:17:57.289 --> 01:17:59.456
I couldn't done this well,

01:18:00.539 --> 01:18:02.456
but I managed to do it.

01:18:03.543 --> 01:18:07.176
They know their level and
they want to progress to good.

01:18:07.176 --> 01:18:09.276
Everybody wants to do a good episode,

01:18:09.276 --> 01:18:10.773
want to make a quality.

01:18:10.773 --> 01:18:14.627
But you have to manage it
with the amount of scheduled,

01:18:14.627 --> 01:18:16.528
the amount of money.

01:18:16.528 --> 01:18:19.236
And yes, it's very hard.

01:18:19.236 --> 01:18:21.333
And sometime you, as I mentioned,

01:18:21.333 --> 01:18:22.666
a good schedule,

01:18:24.703 --> 01:18:28.269
there's something going
well doesn't exist.

01:18:28.269 --> 01:18:31.352
You have a lot of programs
you have to adjust.

01:18:31.352 --> 01:18:33.491
- It's not just like the
problem of like, you know,

01:18:33.491 --> 01:18:34.833
the single animator, right.

01:18:34.833 --> 01:18:36.018
It's like, there's a lot of things

01:18:36.018 --> 01:18:37.564
that the animator probably has to juggle.

01:18:37.564 --> 01:18:39.794
But like, if I like, you
know, but say for example,

01:18:39.794 --> 01:18:42.065
like, I would maybe
understand a little more

01:18:42.065 --> 01:18:44.666
if even the animator
looked at what they did

01:18:44.666 --> 01:18:46.614
and was like, "Yeah, that
wasn't my best work."

01:18:46.614 --> 01:18:48.425
But this is "Attack on
Titan" we're talking about.

01:18:48.425 --> 01:18:50.571
And it's been pretty amazing so far.

01:18:50.571 --> 01:18:52.848
- Have you been following the
episodes of "Attack on Titan?"

01:18:52.848 --> 01:18:54.711
- Yes, I have watched the last one.

01:18:54.711 --> 01:18:57.989
- People are for some reason
very vocal about like,

01:18:57.989 --> 01:18:58.929
"Oh, it's terrible now.

01:18:58.929 --> 01:19:01.024
"The animation quality is terrible."

01:19:01.024 --> 01:19:04.490
- Most of the people don't
like the CGI, I think, yeah.

01:19:04.490 --> 01:19:07.311
And yeah, if you are used to something

01:19:07.311 --> 01:19:09.978
that you wish that you had done.

01:19:12.031 --> 01:19:13.565
And now it's with CGI.

01:19:13.565 --> 01:19:17.562
Actually me too when I
see, oh, this season's CGI.

01:19:17.562 --> 01:19:20.128
I prefer it was more sakuga.

01:19:20.128 --> 01:19:21.291
I understand.

01:19:21.291 --> 01:19:24.068
- But you can say that because
you're in the industry.

01:19:24.068 --> 01:19:25.026
- Yeah, I understand that.

01:19:25.026 --> 01:19:27.859
Some of them say, "Oh, it's CGI.

01:19:27.859 --> 01:19:29.135
"I prefer sakuga."

01:19:29.135 --> 01:19:31.196
But it's not a reason to-

01:19:31.196 --> 01:19:33.304
- Yeah, it's not a reason to death threat.

01:19:33.304 --> 01:19:34.289
- People are like, "The show is ruined.

01:19:34.289 --> 01:19:36.706
"The CGI has ruined my show."

01:19:36.706 --> 01:19:38.719
And it's like, what do you mean?

01:19:38.719 --> 01:19:39.552
It's so bizarre.

01:19:39.552 --> 01:19:40.623
- But like, people are also complaining

01:19:40.623 --> 01:19:42.438
about some of the sakuga as well.

01:19:42.438 --> 01:19:43.271
- Really?

01:19:43.271 --> 01:19:44.538
- Yeah, I've been seeing
that, like, you know,

01:19:44.538 --> 01:19:46.615
I've seen some people on Twitter-

01:19:46.615 --> 01:19:47.734
- They've been awesome though.

01:19:47.734 --> 01:19:48.567
- Yeah, I know.

01:19:48.567 --> 01:19:50.310
Some people on Twitter have,
you know, like done comparisons

01:19:50.310 --> 01:19:52.355
with like the manga panels, for example.

01:19:52.355 --> 01:19:54.138
And being like, "It's completely ruined!

01:19:54.138 --> 01:19:55.447
"It's not exactly the same."

01:19:55.447 --> 01:19:57.621
Like, how do you feel
about stuff like that?

01:19:57.621 --> 01:19:58.644
(Ken sighs)

01:19:58.644 --> 01:19:59.477
- They push too much.

01:19:59.477 --> 01:20:00.530
(everyone laughs)

01:20:00.530 --> 01:20:01.743
- 'Cause I've always wondered

01:20:01.743 --> 01:20:04.545
'cause you've worked on some
pretty high profile shows.

01:20:04.545 --> 01:20:05.824
- "My Hero" had this problem as well.

01:20:05.824 --> 01:20:07.147
- "My Hero" had this problem a lot.

01:20:07.147 --> 01:20:08.995
- Do you ever, like, when working on it,

01:20:08.995 --> 01:20:10.100
do you ever like feel the pressure

01:20:10.100 --> 01:20:12.071
whenever you're working on a big IP?

01:20:12.071 --> 01:20:13.881
Like, you need to and want to deliver?

01:20:13.881 --> 01:20:16.548
- Actually, I know that most of,

01:20:18.163 --> 01:20:22.718
when I post something
of my genga on Twitter,

01:20:22.718 --> 01:20:25.162
it's not my animation that have likes,

01:20:25.162 --> 01:20:27.868
it's more the IP has likes.

01:20:27.868 --> 01:20:28.917
- Right, right, right.

01:20:28.917 --> 01:20:31.676
- I think people don't, I don't know,

01:20:31.676 --> 01:20:35.350
most of the people puts
a like or the retweet

01:20:35.350 --> 01:20:37.470
because it's my, I like this IP.

01:20:37.470 --> 01:20:38.428
- Yeah, no-

01:20:38.428 --> 01:20:40.909
- "Jojo" fans, right?

01:20:40.909 --> 01:20:42.270
- I did see on your Twitter.

01:20:42.270 --> 01:20:45.025
- Actually yeah, I think
it was my "Jojo" genga-

01:20:45.025 --> 01:20:45.983
- Of course it was!

01:20:45.983 --> 01:20:48.126
- Had the most retweets.

01:20:48.126 --> 01:20:49.709
- Was it the Pesci?

01:20:50.635 --> 01:20:53.516
'Cause I think I saw the
animation that you did for that.

01:20:53.516 --> 01:20:55.712
- Yeah, Bucciarati versus Pesci.

01:20:55.712 --> 01:20:56.750
- I love that!

01:20:56.750 --> 01:20:58.561
That's like literally like
the best fight in part four,

01:20:58.561 --> 01:21:01.087
like so good, it was amazing.

01:21:01.087 --> 01:21:02.554
- It was so hard to-

01:21:02.554 --> 01:21:03.518
(everyone laughs)

01:21:03.518 --> 01:21:05.435
Because it was in 2018.

01:21:07.855 --> 01:21:09.441
It was Christmas.

01:21:09.441 --> 01:21:12.454
And I spent all my Christmas
and New Year working

01:21:12.454 --> 01:21:13.977
at the studio.

01:21:13.977 --> 01:21:16.994
I spent three weeks sleeping
at the studio to finish.

01:21:16.994 --> 01:21:18.822
- Three weeks sleeping at the studio?

01:21:18.822 --> 01:21:19.780
- Yeah.

01:21:19.780 --> 01:21:20.695
- For the Pesci fight?

01:21:20.695 --> 01:21:23.705
- Well, because I had to
finish the "Hero Aca" layout

01:21:23.705 --> 01:21:25.607
and after "Hero Aca" I had my-

01:21:25.607 --> 01:21:27.978
- Wait, so you were working
on the "Hero Aca" layout

01:21:27.978 --> 01:21:29.721
while you're working on the "Jojo" genga?

01:21:29.721 --> 01:21:32.105
- When I finished "Hero
Aca," "Jojo" came back.

01:21:32.105 --> 01:21:34.219
(everyone laughs)

01:21:34.219 --> 01:21:38.052
And the deadline was
like the 10th of January.

01:21:39.983 --> 01:21:44.983
And so most of my coworkers
went to what was a Tapiko.

01:21:45.163 --> 01:21:47.539
So most of it was French people.

01:21:47.539 --> 01:21:49.117
So they went back to France.

01:21:49.117 --> 01:21:52.361
I spend the new year and I came back,

01:21:52.361 --> 01:21:55.588
and when they went to France,

01:21:55.588 --> 01:21:59.361
I had no beard and when they
came back I had a big beard.

01:21:59.361 --> 01:22:01.194
(everyone laughs)

01:22:01.194 --> 01:22:02.491
- Just haven't left the office.

01:22:02.491 --> 01:22:03.789
- I haven't left the office.

01:22:03.789 --> 01:22:04.921
- Just, like, became a hermit.

01:22:04.921 --> 01:22:07.214
(everyone laughs)

01:22:07.214 --> 01:22:11.297
- And so I was going to
go gym to have my shower.

01:22:12.622 --> 01:22:14.149
(everyone laughs)

01:22:14.149 --> 01:22:15.378
- Oh my God.

01:22:15.378 --> 01:22:17.777
- So, that must have been
like the case where like

01:22:17.777 --> 01:22:20.541
if you were there all the
time, you're probably like,

01:22:20.541 --> 01:22:22.305
were you just thinking about
it in the shower as well?

01:22:22.305 --> 01:22:23.166
You're like thinking

01:22:23.166 --> 01:22:25.140
about what you were going
to draw next as well?

01:22:25.140 --> 01:22:27.643
- Yeah, shower takes time,

01:22:27.643 --> 01:22:30.865
but sometimes you can itch or I smell bad.

01:22:30.865 --> 01:22:33.571
I have to take a shower

01:22:33.571 --> 01:22:34.728
- You gotta optimize your showers.

01:22:34.728 --> 01:22:36.816
It's just like, do you
ever get to the point

01:22:36.816 --> 01:22:38.523
when you're just like eating?

01:22:38.523 --> 01:22:40.356
Too much time.

01:22:40.356 --> 01:22:42.991
- I was eating, watching an episode,

01:22:42.991 --> 01:22:45.324
eating and okay, episode finished.

01:22:45.324 --> 01:22:46.309
I finish to eat.

01:22:46.309 --> 01:22:47.582
Okay, go back to work.

01:22:47.582 --> 01:22:49.040
- Jesus.

01:22:49.040 --> 01:22:50.467
- You're welcome "Jojo" fans.

01:22:50.467 --> 01:22:51.539
(everyone laughs)

01:22:51.539 --> 01:22:53.543
- You're welcome anime fans.

01:22:53.543 --> 01:22:56.736
- And so, yes, I get sick also.

01:22:56.736 --> 01:23:00.819
I think I had, eat a bad
one or I have influenza,

01:23:02.350 --> 01:23:03.482
how do you say in English?

01:23:03.482 --> 01:23:04.315
- You had influenza?

01:23:04.315 --> 01:23:05.484
- Yeah, I get influenza this time.

01:23:05.484 --> 01:23:07.317
- You got flu.

01:23:07.317 --> 01:23:08.921
- I was working like that.

01:23:08.921 --> 01:23:10.439
(Ken groans)

01:23:10.439 --> 01:23:14.670
- Literally killing
yourself for "Jojo" fans.

01:23:14.670 --> 01:23:15.777
- You can say you were.

01:23:15.777 --> 01:23:16.929
(everyone laughs)

01:23:16.929 --> 01:23:18.135
I think you can say it.

01:23:18.135 --> 01:23:20.574
- I was trying to do my best on this one.

01:23:20.574 --> 01:23:22.138
- I think a lot of people would argue

01:23:22.138 --> 01:23:24.526
that's one of the best
fight scenes in part five.

01:23:24.526 --> 01:23:26.788
It looks amazing as well.

01:23:26.788 --> 01:23:28.849
- I think all of part
five, everyone could tell-

01:23:28.849 --> 01:23:31.086
- Not just saying that 'cause
you're here. (everyone laughs)

01:23:31.086 --> 01:23:32.378
- Yeah, no, it's definitely
a crowd favorite.

01:23:32.378 --> 01:23:35.944
- Like I said, animations is a teamwork.

01:23:35.944 --> 01:23:38.538
So like I said, I do the rough animation

01:23:38.538 --> 01:23:40.655
after the director put some correction.

01:23:40.655 --> 01:23:43.972
So something that was a
too little, how can I say?

01:23:43.972 --> 01:23:45.942
Oh, you can push more this arm.

01:23:45.942 --> 01:23:47.673
The director will put it in.

01:23:47.673 --> 01:23:52.256
After the director of animation
will put more in model.

01:23:53.995 --> 01:23:57.017
And so these three tips
are very important.

01:23:57.017 --> 01:24:00.193
After I have received this
correction, I redraw it,

01:24:00.193 --> 01:24:01.624
everything with all the detail,

01:24:01.624 --> 01:24:05.373
all the shadows, all the
light, all the perfect frames.

01:24:05.373 --> 01:24:07.009
So yes, it's a teamwork.

01:24:07.009 --> 01:24:08.150
And after these drawings,

01:24:08.150 --> 01:24:11.937
it will be the in-betweener
who will cleanup.

01:24:11.937 --> 01:24:14.527
And it's a very teamwork.

01:24:14.527 --> 01:24:17.062
It's not just one animator's work,

01:24:17.062 --> 01:24:18.680
it's you have the director,

01:24:18.680 --> 01:24:22.803
the director of animation,
the in-betweener, the color.

01:24:22.803 --> 01:24:25.534
- I'm curious, this is
gonna be a dumb question.

01:24:25.534 --> 01:24:28.222
Do you like hear, when you're drawing it,

01:24:28.222 --> 01:24:30.621
I assume is the voice acting
recorded at that point?

01:24:30.621 --> 01:24:31.930
Or is it not recorded?

01:24:31.930 --> 01:24:33.217
- No, it's way after.

01:24:33.217 --> 01:24:34.050
- Way after?

01:24:34.050 --> 01:24:34.883
Oh, wow.

01:24:34.883 --> 01:24:35.716
- The voice acting is post-production.

01:24:35.716 --> 01:24:38.048
- Oh, wow. So you don't even
get to, like, hear the lines

01:24:38.048 --> 01:24:39.573
as you're drawing or anything.

01:24:39.573 --> 01:24:43.236
- Sometimes you have some rough voice.

01:24:43.236 --> 01:24:46.277
But it's not the final voice.

01:24:46.277 --> 01:24:47.687
- It's mostly just, like,

01:24:47.687 --> 01:24:50.513
I think it's written out in
the layout section, right?

01:24:50.513 --> 01:24:52.040
Of what the actual what they're gonna say

01:24:52.040 --> 01:24:52.873
in this particular-

01:24:52.873 --> 01:24:54.081
- The storyboard.

01:24:54.081 --> 01:24:55.419
And after you have the time sheet

01:24:55.419 --> 01:24:58.542
when at this moment you have to.

01:24:58.542 --> 01:25:00.438
- And then the voice actors match that.

01:25:00.438 --> 01:25:01.271
- Yeah.

01:25:01.271 --> 01:25:02.815
- So all anime is dubbed anime.

01:25:02.815 --> 01:25:04.404
- Yeah, it is dubbed.

01:25:04.404 --> 01:25:05.936
(everyone laughs)

01:25:05.936 --> 01:25:06.769
- Wow.

01:25:07.644 --> 01:25:08.744
- Checkmate, sub-elitists.

01:25:08.744 --> 01:25:10.738
(everyone laughs)

01:25:10.738 --> 01:25:11.982
I've always been curious

01:25:11.982 --> 01:25:13.240
because obviously like you work

01:25:13.240 --> 01:25:14.828
on a lot of shonen jump properties

01:25:14.828 --> 01:25:18.689
and that's obviously based on
like adapting manga panels.

01:25:18.689 --> 01:25:21.189
As an animator, do you ever like look

01:25:21.189 --> 01:25:23.407
at the manga panels of, like,
the cut you're animating?

01:25:23.407 --> 01:25:25.110
Or do you just try to go in fresh?

01:25:25.110 --> 01:25:26.776
- Yeah, of course. So
when I do the meetings,

01:25:26.776 --> 01:25:31.776
I have the manga on my side
because they have print manga.

01:25:32.040 --> 01:25:32.873
- Okay.

01:25:32.873 --> 01:25:34.607
- Your scene will be on
this part of the manga.

01:25:34.607 --> 01:25:35.815
They give it to me.

01:25:35.815 --> 01:25:40.168
And so, yes, it's important
to read a bit of the manga

01:25:40.168 --> 01:25:44.087
because you more know
how is the characters.

01:25:44.087 --> 01:25:46.957
And also when you speak with the director,

01:25:46.957 --> 01:25:49.219
he will say so this
character is more calm.

01:25:49.219 --> 01:25:51.545
He doesn't have much expression.

01:25:51.545 --> 01:25:53.424
And so don't,

01:25:53.424 --> 01:25:55.424
less cold man, ice face.

01:25:56.355 --> 01:25:58.507
- I guess you got to know the
personality of the character

01:25:58.507 --> 01:25:59.340
to know how they-

01:25:59.340 --> 01:26:00.173
- Yes.

01:26:00.173 --> 01:26:03.939
So if you have read the
manga, it's a good job

01:26:03.939 --> 01:26:06.313
because, well, the director will be,

01:26:06.313 --> 01:26:08.916
"Oh, he has read the manga,
so he knows the show."

01:26:08.916 --> 01:26:09.819
- [Connor] Right, that makes sense.

01:26:09.819 --> 01:26:12.176
- So all animators are manga readers.

01:26:12.176 --> 01:26:13.585
- No, it depends.

01:26:13.585 --> 01:26:15.252
Some times I didn't.

01:26:16.393 --> 01:26:18.645
Wait, I read everything.

01:26:18.645 --> 01:26:21.255
(everyone laughs)

01:26:21.255 --> 01:26:23.978
- Just proving your own point.

01:26:23.978 --> 01:26:27.061
- My buddy Medi hadn't read the show.

01:26:29.064 --> 01:26:31.773
And so we bet he walked out on it so-so.

01:26:31.773 --> 01:26:33.503
- I guess then in that sense,

01:26:33.503 --> 01:26:36.648
I guess like anime
originals must be so hard,

01:26:36.648 --> 01:26:37.981
so much harder because there's no-

01:26:37.981 --> 01:26:40.028
- Oh yeah, there's no reference point.

01:26:40.028 --> 01:26:41.500
- Like, light novels I guess even.

01:26:41.500 --> 01:26:42.828
- But even still, right?

01:26:42.828 --> 01:26:45.557
Like, light novels would be
even harder because you gotta-

01:26:45.557 --> 01:26:46.462
- It's just all words.

01:26:46.462 --> 01:26:47.545
- It's all text.

01:26:47.545 --> 01:26:49.752
- If you want a good fact,

01:26:49.752 --> 01:26:52.711
when I was working on
"Dragon Ball Super Broly"

01:26:52.711 --> 01:26:54.420
I didn't know it was Broly.

01:26:54.420 --> 01:26:55.253
- Oh, really?

01:26:55.253 --> 01:26:56.336
- Who'd you think it was?

01:26:56.336 --> 01:26:58.415
- I was working on the "Dragon Ball" movie

01:26:58.415 --> 01:27:00.539
but I didn't know it was the bad guy.

01:27:00.539 --> 01:27:03.226
(everyone laughs)

01:27:03.226 --> 01:27:04.667
- 'Cause you didn't read it.

01:27:04.667 --> 01:27:07.096
- No because he didn't say to me.

01:27:07.096 --> 01:27:09.423
- Oh, they're just like, "Draw this."

01:27:09.423 --> 01:27:11.992
- Wait, they kept the fact
that Broly was a bad guy

01:27:11.992 --> 01:27:13.464
from the animators?

01:27:13.464 --> 01:27:16.873
- It was a secret that
I didn't know the title

01:27:16.873 --> 01:27:18.848
of the show was "Broly."

01:27:18.848 --> 01:27:20.434
- Oh, so you animated that

01:27:20.434 --> 01:27:24.304
without even knowing the
context of the entire cut.

01:27:24.304 --> 01:27:25.137
- Yeah.

01:27:25.137 --> 01:27:26.444
- You were just like, "Oh, sick, Broly!"

01:27:26.444 --> 01:27:27.740
(everyone laughs)

01:27:27.740 --> 01:27:29.179
- Because I have phone-

01:27:29.179 --> 01:27:30.012
- That sounds insane.

01:27:30.012 --> 01:27:34.679
- Because my cut was just
Vegeta was going against Goku.

01:27:35.694 --> 01:27:37.249
- Oh, okay.

01:27:37.249 --> 01:27:42.158
- So, yes, and I think
they didn't want some leaks

01:27:42.158 --> 01:27:44.360
about Broly.
- I mean, that makes sense.

01:27:44.360 --> 01:27:47.013
- I mean, you know, they
could also just sign an NDA.

01:27:47.013 --> 01:27:50.213
(everyone laughs)

01:27:50.213 --> 01:27:51.796
- What?

01:27:51.796 --> 01:27:53.397
- Never heard of it.

01:27:53.397 --> 01:27:55.661
- I'm curious, this is
just such a vague question.

01:27:55.661 --> 01:27:59.638
What is your like top anime
shows for you personally?

01:27:59.638 --> 01:28:00.903
- Original anime show?

01:28:00.903 --> 01:28:02.315
- Anything.

01:28:02.315 --> 01:28:04.603
- I prefer to talk about original anime

01:28:04.603 --> 01:28:07.036
because, well, when it's adaptation,

01:28:07.036 --> 01:28:09.583
you have multiple of the manga.

01:28:09.583 --> 01:28:13.821
So maybe, I like "Evangelion" like I said,

01:28:13.821 --> 01:28:15.149
and "Gurren Lagann."

01:28:15.149 --> 01:28:17.566
- "Gurren Lagann," of course.

01:28:19.737 --> 01:28:22.205
- It's just a little like guy next trio.

01:28:22.205 --> 01:28:25.747
- Because they had the power
to do original animation

01:28:25.747 --> 01:28:27.009
and it was great.

01:28:27.009 --> 01:28:31.342
After I don't watch much
of them, much shows before.

01:28:33.230 --> 01:28:34.851
- Too busy making them.

01:28:34.851 --> 01:28:38.024
- And also when you ask
"Oh, what's your top 10?"

01:28:38.024 --> 01:28:39.535
You forgot.

01:28:39.535 --> 01:28:41.105
- No, we're exactly the same.

01:28:41.105 --> 01:28:43.030
- I put you on the spot, I'm sorry.

01:28:43.030 --> 01:28:44.184
- I do want to know though

01:28:44.184 --> 01:28:47.055
as an animator are there any, like, scenes

01:28:47.055 --> 01:28:49.982
or any animation cuts
that you really look up to

01:28:49.982 --> 01:28:53.928
and you, like, idolize as
legendary and have inspired you?

01:28:53.928 --> 01:28:55.511
- Yeah.

01:28:55.511 --> 01:28:58.594
Like, you have a lot of animation of,

01:29:00.812 --> 01:29:03.729
"Wow, how he make these movements?"

01:29:05.292 --> 01:29:09.189
And so, yeah, when you're
doing frame per frame

01:29:09.189 --> 01:29:11.124
when you're animator,

01:29:11.124 --> 01:29:12.128
watch the movement.

01:29:12.128 --> 01:29:16.386
Okay, oh, this frame is
just exposed at one, two.

01:29:16.386 --> 01:29:18.513
Oh, this frame, is exposed at three.

01:29:18.513 --> 01:29:21.375
And oh, at this moment you
have the fire come here.

01:29:21.375 --> 01:29:25.722
And you analyze the movement
like that frame by frame.

01:29:25.722 --> 01:29:27.837
Every animator's doing like that.

01:29:27.837 --> 01:29:31.396
And so, oh, so this is the key animation.

01:29:31.396 --> 01:29:33.255
- So, you watch the anime really slow.

01:29:33.255 --> 01:29:35.240
(everyone laughs)

01:29:35.240 --> 01:29:39.169
- At first I watch the
anime like everybody.

01:29:39.169 --> 01:29:40.459
Whoa, what was his movement?

01:29:40.459 --> 01:29:43.110
So I put a stop and frame
by frame by frame by frame.

01:29:43.110 --> 01:29:45.544
- I guess like an animator
or I guess like director

01:29:45.544 --> 01:29:47.292
that comes to mind when it comes to, like,

01:29:47.292 --> 01:29:49.992
amazing animation would be
like Satoshi Kon, right?

01:29:49.992 --> 01:29:51.075
- Yeah.

01:29:51.075 --> 01:29:52.982
You know Kon Satoshi.

01:29:52.982 --> 01:29:56.177
- Like, Kon Satoshi, like, he
managed to animate in a way,

01:29:56.177 --> 01:29:58.532
because I think I saw it in
some kind of interview with him,

01:29:58.532 --> 01:30:00.448
like way before,

01:30:00.448 --> 01:30:03.136
that, like, the reason why
he went into animation was

01:30:03.136 --> 01:30:07.486
because his way of directing
is too fast for live action.

01:30:07.486 --> 01:30:08.319
- Yeah.

01:30:08.319 --> 01:30:09.152
- So, whereas like,

01:30:09.152 --> 01:30:11.196
because there's so many cuts in Kon movies

01:30:11.196 --> 01:30:12.860
where it's just, it's like a blink.

01:30:12.860 --> 01:30:14.962
It's so fast, it's almost subliminal

01:30:14.962 --> 01:30:17.713
that you just can't
replicate in live action.

01:30:17.713 --> 01:30:18.770
And he's just, I dunno.

01:30:18.770 --> 01:30:21.117
Like, even I'm not an
animator at all or anything

01:30:21.117 --> 01:30:24.306
but like you can watch a
Satoshi Kon movie and be like,

01:30:24.306 --> 01:30:26.992
how do you even think to
animate something like that?

01:30:26.992 --> 01:30:29.317
- I have one of my senpai who had worked

01:30:29.317 --> 01:30:31.038
on a Kon Satoshi movie.

01:30:31.038 --> 01:30:34.788
It was the co-director
of "Tokyo Godfathers."

01:30:36.062 --> 01:30:37.145
- Oh wow.

01:30:37.145 --> 01:30:40.048
- His name is Furuya Shogo.

01:30:40.048 --> 01:30:43.715
And yeah, the Kon movies
are very realistic.

01:30:46.079 --> 01:30:49.662
Realistic in the
character, the expression.

01:30:52.921 --> 01:30:54.071
In "Millennium Actress,"

01:30:54.071 --> 01:30:58.836
the way he mix up the fiction
and reality is so good.

01:30:58.836 --> 01:30:59.995
- It's like the scene transitions.

01:30:59.995 --> 01:31:02.101
It's just like nuts.

01:31:02.101 --> 01:31:04.645
- And you can watch it every time and,

01:31:04.645 --> 01:31:07.645
oh, this cut connects with this cut.

01:31:08.583 --> 01:31:11.038
And also I like "Tokyo Godfathers"

01:31:11.038 --> 01:31:13.953
because I dunno, it's a
movie you want to watch

01:31:13.953 --> 01:31:15.028
at Christmas.

01:31:15.028 --> 01:31:18.609
- It's one of the few
Christmas anime movies, I feel.

01:31:18.609 --> 01:31:21.526
Not that it was meant to
be a Christmas anime movie.

01:31:21.526 --> 01:31:23.865
It just happens to be on Christmas.

01:31:23.865 --> 01:31:28.420
- And yeah, but one, my senpai
said Kon Satoshi was one

01:31:28.420 --> 01:31:31.562
of the best maybe best anime.

01:31:31.562 --> 01:31:32.395
- Oh yeah.

01:31:32.395 --> 01:31:33.949
- He's really, really fast.

01:31:33.949 --> 01:31:36.282
And he have a perfect brain.

01:31:37.643 --> 01:31:39.132
(Connor laughs)

01:31:39.132 --> 01:31:40.745
- Yeah, because I think I saw that, like,

01:31:40.745 --> 01:31:44.177
Satoshi Kon used to like draw
some of his own animations

01:31:44.177 --> 01:31:45.010
as well.

01:31:45.010 --> 01:31:46.440
He was key animator of his own show.

01:31:46.440 --> 01:31:48.761
- Because he have done mangaka.

01:31:48.761 --> 01:31:50.344
Yes, he was manga.

01:31:51.997 --> 01:31:54.648
Lot of work with Katsuhiro Otomo.

01:31:54.648 --> 01:31:55.481
- Yeah, yeah.

01:31:55.481 --> 01:31:58.084
- And so yeah, I don't
know if he have work

01:31:58.084 --> 01:31:59.276
on "Akira" or not.

01:31:59.276 --> 01:32:00.382
I don't remember.

01:32:00.382 --> 01:32:02.489
But yes, he was very close with Otomo

01:32:02.489 --> 01:32:05.156
with those generation of artists

01:32:06.035 --> 01:32:09.285
who was a lot of movie makers in Japan.

01:32:10.398 --> 01:32:11.475
- As an animator, what do you think

01:32:11.475 --> 01:32:13.630
of like "Akira" for
instance, like the animation?

01:32:13.630 --> 01:32:15.702
- "Akira" is amazing animation.

01:32:15.702 --> 01:32:18.592
- Because I feel that like,
when people say "Akira,"

01:32:18.592 --> 01:32:20.713
they're just like, yeah,
this animation hasn't aged.

01:32:20.713 --> 01:32:22.546
Like, it aged so well.

01:32:23.401 --> 01:32:27.568
- If you want a bit for
animators, good animation,

01:32:29.787 --> 01:32:31.455
you have so "Jin-Roh."

01:32:31.455 --> 01:32:32.663
- "Jin-Roh."

01:32:32.663 --> 01:32:34.527
- I've heard that's pretty legendary.

01:32:34.527 --> 01:32:37.740
- For my senpai he said that
"Jin-Roh" is to animation,

01:32:37.740 --> 01:32:39.990
realistic the most extreme.

01:32:41.100 --> 01:32:43.979
Too much extreme that most
of the animators is just

01:32:43.979 --> 01:32:46.072
for masturbation of animation.

01:32:46.072 --> 01:32:49.064
(everyone laughs)

01:32:49.064 --> 01:32:50.504
It's too much.

01:32:50.504 --> 01:32:53.001
But he said, it's a
good entertainment one.

01:32:53.001 --> 01:32:54.979
And with the good animation

01:32:54.979 --> 01:32:57.729
or so very pushed was "Memories."

01:32:58.991 --> 01:33:00.454
- [Joey] The ultima Katsuhiro.

01:33:00.454 --> 01:33:03.148
- And you have the "Magnetic Rose."

01:33:03.148 --> 01:33:06.081
- "Magnetic Rose" is so good.
- I don't know any of these.

01:33:06.081 --> 01:33:07.646
- Each plan of "Magnetic Rose"

01:33:07.646 --> 01:33:09.437
of animation is a masterclass.

01:33:09.437 --> 01:33:14.187
Because most of the frames
are exposition of three frame.

01:33:17.006 --> 01:33:21.006
Less frame but just good
drawings, good timings.

01:33:22.103 --> 01:33:24.295
- "Magnetic Rose" if
you don't know is, like,

01:33:24.295 --> 01:33:25.935
a space opera "Akira."

01:33:25.935 --> 01:33:27.135
That's the only way to describe it.

01:33:27.135 --> 01:33:29.123
- How old is it?

01:33:29.123 --> 01:33:29.959
- How old is it?

01:33:29.959 --> 01:33:31.909
It's like from the 90s?

01:33:31.909 --> 01:33:33.744
Like, late 90s.

01:33:33.744 --> 01:33:35.994
It was quite a while after,

01:33:35.994 --> 01:33:38.795
but it's like, "Magnetic
Rose" is like a short film

01:33:38.795 --> 01:33:40.613
that Otomo Katsuhiro directed.

01:33:40.613 --> 01:33:41.712
- It's like 40 minute-

01:33:41.712 --> 01:33:43.238
- It's like a 40 minute short film,

01:33:43.238 --> 01:33:44.418
but it's like, yeah,

01:33:44.418 --> 01:33:47.696
it's basically just space
opera "Akira" is the only way

01:33:47.696 --> 01:33:49.746
to describe it, but it's fucking amazing.

01:33:49.746 --> 01:33:52.110
- And with the same
team of "Magnetic Rose,"

01:33:52.110 --> 01:33:55.618
you have a "Hashire Melos," "Run, Melos."

01:33:55.618 --> 01:33:56.884
I didn't to watch it

01:33:56.884 --> 01:34:00.541
but I had watched some
cuts of "Hashire Melo"

01:34:00.541 --> 01:34:02.010
and it was very impressive.

01:34:02.010 --> 01:34:03.468
So yeah.

01:34:03.468 --> 01:34:07.615
- So I guess if you want to be
an animator just study those.

01:34:07.615 --> 01:34:09.645
- This is the realist ones,

01:34:09.645 --> 01:34:12.537
the golden age of animators, we say.

01:34:12.537 --> 01:34:14.610
- It's interesting
hearing an actual opinion

01:34:14.610 --> 01:34:15.961
from an actual animator.

01:34:15.961 --> 01:34:19.286
'Cause you know, whenever
we think of like,

01:34:19.286 --> 01:34:20.888
oh, what do we think is the best animated

01:34:20.888 --> 01:34:23.024
whatever or anime of all time?

01:34:23.024 --> 01:34:26.299
Like, most people would say
like "Redline" probably.

01:34:26.299 --> 01:34:28.218
The one that comes to my mind.

01:34:28.218 --> 01:34:29.176
- Definitely.

01:34:29.176 --> 01:34:30.254
- Do you think that,

01:34:30.254 --> 01:34:35.097
what's your opinion about
like older anime versus, like,

01:34:35.097 --> 01:34:36.621
newer digitized anime?

01:34:36.621 --> 01:34:37.454
- Yeah.

01:34:38.454 --> 01:34:42.287
Well, digital animation
is you can get quicker

01:34:43.576 --> 01:34:45.647
because we can work at to your place

01:34:45.647 --> 01:34:48.147
and send by mail or the datas.

01:34:49.201 --> 01:34:50.371
It's not paper.

01:34:50.371 --> 01:34:51.562
You don't have to scan it.

01:34:51.562 --> 01:34:55.395
But the program offered
the animation industry

01:34:56.448 --> 01:35:01.189
to most of, like I said,
sakans, animation director.

01:35:01.189 --> 01:35:03.563
Most of them are on paper.

01:35:03.563 --> 01:35:05.618
- Because they've been in
the industry for so long.

01:35:05.618 --> 01:35:08.352
- So long and they would like

01:35:08.352 --> 01:35:11.105
to learn some digital animation,

01:35:11.105 --> 01:35:13.691
but they don't have the time.

01:35:13.691 --> 01:35:15.774
Yeah, or they don't care.

01:35:16.712 --> 01:35:18.992
- Paper is superior.

01:35:18.992 --> 01:35:21.436
- I work in 10 years and will die so.

01:35:21.436 --> 01:35:23.092
(everyone laughs)

01:35:23.092 --> 01:35:25.952
- I'll die doing animation on paper!

01:35:25.952 --> 01:35:27.056
- I learned animation on paper,

01:35:27.056 --> 01:35:28.917
I will die doing animation on paper.

01:35:28.917 --> 01:35:32.435
- Some of my senpai have tried
to learn digital animation,

01:35:32.435 --> 01:35:36.257
but he was too much stress
that he have a pain on stomach.

01:35:36.257 --> 01:35:38.090
Had to go to hospital.

01:35:39.240 --> 01:35:40.120
- Oh God.

01:35:40.120 --> 01:35:42.953
(everyone laughs)

01:35:43.795 --> 01:35:46.975
- That's horrible, but I just
have to laugh about that.

01:35:46.975 --> 01:35:49.892
- So yeah, so me I'm doing digital.

01:35:52.048 --> 01:35:54.222
And so I'm doing my layout in digital.

01:35:54.222 --> 01:35:56.610
But if the sakan have to
check it, put correction,

01:35:56.610 --> 01:36:00.027
they have to print it and put correction.

01:36:02.306 --> 01:36:03.523
- And then fax it back to you.

01:36:03.523 --> 01:36:04.356
- Yeah.

01:36:04.356 --> 01:36:07.455
(everyone laughs)

01:36:07.455 --> 01:36:09.663
- That was a joke, right?

01:36:09.663 --> 01:36:10.629
- This wasn't a joke.

01:36:10.629 --> 01:36:12.069
(everyone laughs)

01:36:12.069 --> 01:36:14.373
- I was joking, oh God.

01:36:14.373 --> 01:36:17.135
- Because they have the
correction is on paper.

01:36:17.135 --> 01:36:20.001
No, no, sorry, but they have to print it.

01:36:20.001 --> 01:36:20.959
They scan it.

01:36:20.959 --> 01:36:23.883
They scan it to send it me back by data.

01:36:23.883 --> 01:36:26.592
And for me to doing it digital.

01:36:26.592 --> 01:36:30.592
So yeah, so most of the
in-betweens are digital,

01:36:32.511 --> 01:36:34.166
but it depends.

01:36:34.166 --> 01:36:37.044
So digital and paper are a bit.

01:36:37.044 --> 01:36:41.920
I think more veterans and good
animators are still on paper.

01:36:41.920 --> 01:36:44.715
Nowadays some youngs are more on digital,

01:36:44.715 --> 01:36:47.526
but the problem is software.

01:36:47.526 --> 01:36:49.262
You have to pay it.

01:36:49.262 --> 01:36:52.512
And most of the software are expensive.

01:36:54.095 --> 01:36:55.878
- Commercial licenses are very expensive.

01:36:55.878 --> 01:36:59.961
- And also, you know how
much animators are paid.

01:37:02.149 --> 01:37:06.616
There is good stuff like
TVPaint, but it's too expensive.

01:37:06.616 --> 01:37:07.449
So yeah.

01:37:09.575 --> 01:37:11.947
- I can't believe the
software's, like, too expensive

01:37:11.947 --> 01:37:15.728
